@0    = ~I saw you and Faren sneaking off last night. Had a good time?~
@1    = ~Yes, I did. I'm growing very fond of Faren.~
@2    = ~It was a mistake, just a fling. I don't want it to go any further.~
@3    = ~I have no feelings for Faren. I don't know why he's pursuing me like this.~
@4    = ~Indeed. I shall bear that in mind.~
@5    = ~Well, I have been bothering you over this for too long - let's get moving.~
@6    = ~Perhaps he sees something in you - it would not be the first time such a misunderstanding has occurred.~
@7    = ~Anyway, I have been bothering you over this for too long - let's get moving.~
@8    = ~Smelly, filthy and salty. Why do city folk insist on throwing their worst - ugh, was that a rotten fish? - rubbish into the sea?~
@9    = ~Too lazy to do anything else with it, I guess.~
@10   = ~You're looking a little green yourself. Are you all right?~
@11   = ~I get seasick.~
@12   = ~Really? I might have thought you would enjoy swinging from the sails.~
@13   = ~Ugh, don't even talk to me about that, I'm bad enough on the shore...~
@14   = ~All right, I'm fed up with you staring at me. What do you think you're playing at?~
@15   = ~Hmm? Oh - nothing. Sorry.~
@16   = ~Although - your hair looks really nice in the sun. Sort of shiny.~
@17   = ~Although - your hair looks really nice in the moonlight. Sort of shiny.~
@18   = ~Don't be ridiculous, soldier. Now, keep your eyes to yourself.~
@19   = ~I'm kind of good at juggling. You think you could get me into that circus of yours?~
@20   = ~I don't think you'd be quite right for them, soldier. They were very close-knit, like a family. It takes a long time to gain acceptance.~
@21   = ~Damn, there goes another life plan.~
@22   = ~Do you really need such a plan? It's enough to adventure at <CHARNAME>'s side, isn't it? At least, that's what I've heard you saying.~
@23   = ~We-ell, can you keep a secret? Not everything I say to <CHARNAME> is the complete and utter truth.~
@24   = ~Don't worry, I will tell <PRO_HIMHER> no tales.~
